---
import { person } from '../data/resume';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const { '@context': context, ...profile } = person;
---

<Base title="About" description="About Avishek, also known as notDeadCaller." schema={{ '@context': context, '@type': 'ProfilePage', mainEntity: profile }}>
	<header class="page-head">
		<h1 data-decode>About</h1>
		<p>Avishek, also known as notDeadCaller. Based in Kolkata.</p>
	</header>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			I work in offensive security, mostly black-box testing of web applications: no source code, no credentials, only
			what the application exposes. I am most interested in small logic flaws that have large consequences, like a
			login flow that never limits how many times you can guess a one-time password.
		</p>
		<p>
			I also build software. Recent projects include an Android safety app, a private chat over TCP using
			post-quantum cryptography, and a health assistant for university students.
		</p>
		<p>
			This site collects <a href="/writeups/">writeups</a> of security work, shorter <a href="/notes/">notes</a>, and
			<a href="/projects/">projects</a>. If you are here to hire me, start with the <a href="/resume/">resume</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/avishekwithav/">LinkedIn</a> or
			<a href="https://github.com/notDeadCaller">GitHub</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="colophon">Colophon</h2>
		<p>
			Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and hosted on GitHub Pages. The ASCII artwork is drawn live in
			a canvas by a small renderer written for this site. The visual language draws on the interfaces of Watch Dogs and
			Cyberpunk 2077.
		</p>
		<blockquote>{SITE.quote}</blockquote>
	</div>
</Base>
